---
layout: null
permalink: /sitemap.xml
---
{%- comment -%}
================================================================================
  AUTO-GENERATED SITEMAP — do not hand-edit the output, edit this template.

  Every page carrying an `i18n-ref` is emitted automatically, so adding,
  removing or renaming a page updates the sitemap on the next build with no
  manual step. Work-in-progress pages that are not committed simply do not
  exist at build time on GitHub Pages, so they never leak into production.

  Per page it emits:
    <loc>        the canonical URL
    <lastmod>    from the page's `last_modified:` front-matter, auto-advanced
                 to the newest item date on collection-backed index pages
    <image:*>    content images (see the image block below)
    <xhtml:link> hreflang alternates for all four languages, plus x-default
                 pointing at Spanish (the root, default language)

  Opt a page out with `sitemap: false` in its front-matter (used by the 404s).

  `changefreq` and `priority` are deliberately omitted — Google ignores both.
================================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign known_langs = "ca,en,es,ja,it" | split: "," -%}
{%- assign hero_variants = "-1200,-1920,-2560,-2880" | split: "," -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Narrow the static-file list ONCE here rather than re-testing all ~2,800
  files inside every page's loop. /photos/ alone holds the large majority of
  them and can never match, so hoisting this out is the difference between
  roughly 170,000 Liquid iterations per build and roughly 18,000.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign content_images = site.static_files | where: "extname", ".jpg" | where_exp: "f", "f.path contains '/images/'" -%}
{%- assign indexable = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.i18n-ref" | where_exp: "p", "p.sitemap != false" -%}
{%- assign refs = indexable | map: "i18n-ref" | uniq | sort -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9" xmlns:image="http://www.google.com/schemas/sitemap-image/1.1" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
{%- for ref in refs -%}
  {%- assign group = indexable | where: "i18n-ref", ref | sort: "lang" -%}
  {%- assign xdefault = group | where: "lang", "es" | first -%}
  {%- for p in group %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ p.url }}</loc>
    {%- assign lastmod = p.last_modified -%}
    {%- if ref == 'events-hFZ2XXIp' and site.events.size > 0 -%}
      {%- assign newest = site.events | map: 'date_from' | sort | last | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
      {%- assign lastmod = lastmod | append: "," | append: newest | split: "," | sort | last -%}
    {%- elsif ref == 'photos-QDOJ1pyG' and site.photos.size > 0 -%}
      {%- assign raw = site.photos | map: 'date' | sort | last | append: "" -%}
      {%- assign y = raw | slice: 0, 4 -%}{%- assign mo = raw | slice: 4, 2 -%}{%- assign d = raw | slice: 6, 2 -%}
      {%- assign newest = y | append: "-" | append: mo | append: "-" | append: d -%}
      {%- assign lastmod = lastmod | append: "," | append: newest | split: "," | sort | last -%}
    {%- elsif ref == 'videos-NuhYeNWr' and site.videos.size > 0 -%}
      {%- assign raw = site.videos | map: 'date' | sort | last | append: "" -%}
      {%- assign y = raw | slice: 0, 4 -%}{%- assign mo = raw | slice: 4, 2 -%}{%- assign d = raw | slice: 6, 2 -%}
      {%- assign newest = y | append: "-" | append: mo | append: "-" | append: d -%}
      {%- assign lastmod = lastmod | append: "," | append: newest | split: "," | sort | last -%}
    {%- elsif ref == 'resources-uStNjtHz' and site.resources.size > 0 -%}
      {%- assign newest = site.resources | map: 'date' | sort | last | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
      {%- assign lastmod = lastmod | append: "," | append: newest | split: "," | sort | last -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      NEVER IN THE FUTURE.

      The four rules above take the newest item in a collection so that
      publishing one bumps its index page without anyone editing front matter.
      That is right for a photo album, whose date is when it was taken, and
      wrong for a seminar, whose date is when it WILL happen: booking a
      masterclass five months out set the Seminars pages' lastmod to
      2027-01-30. `lastmod` says when the page changed, and a page cannot have
      changed on a day that has not arrived. Google discounts a lastmod it
      decides is unreliable, and a date in the future is the clearest possible
      way to look unreliable.

      Clamping rather than special-casing the events rule: a hand-typed
      `last_modified` in the future is just as wrong, and this catches that too.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Normalised to a string first. An unquoted `last_modified: 2026-09-04` in
      front matter reaches Liquid as a Ruby Date, and comparing a Date with a
      String raises. The collection branches above never hit it because their
      `append: ","` had already coerced the value.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if lastmod %}{% assign lastmod = lastmod | date: '%Y-%m-%d' %}{% endif -%}
    {%- assign build_day = site.time | date: '%Y-%m-%d' -%}
    {%- if lastmod and lastmod > build_day %}{% assign lastmod = build_day %}{% endif -%}
    {%- if lastmod %}
    <lastmod>{{ lastmod }}</lastmod>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Images. Collection-backed pages read the exact filename the page renders
      from front-matter, which keeps the localised titles and honours the
      cross-language fallbacks (e.g. a ja course reusing the en poster).
      Every other page is matched against /images/ by its i18n-ref prefix,
      which the naming convention guarantees.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if ref == 'events-hFZ2XXIp' -%}
      {%- for item in site.events -%}
        {%- case p.lang -%}
          {%- when 'ca' -%}{%- assign img = item.image_ca -%}{%- assign t = item.title_ca -%}
          {%- when 'en' -%}{%- assign img = item.image_en -%}{%- assign t = item.title_en -%}
          {%- when 'ja' -%}{%- assign img = item.image_ja -%}{%- assign t = item.title_ja -%}
          {%- else -%}{%- assign img = item.image_es -%}{%- assign t = item.title_es -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          `img != ''` and not just `img`. An empty string is truthy in Liquid,
          and a seminar whose poster is still being drawn carries `image_es: ""`
          — which emitted <image:loc>…/images/.jpg</image:loc>, a sitemap entry
          for a file that cannot exist. qa.py's sitemap check is what would have
          caught it; this is what stops it being written.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if img and img != '' %}
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>{{ site.url }}/images/{{ img }}.jpg</image:loc>
      <image:title>{{ t | xml_escape }}</image:title>
    </image:image>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- elsif ref == 'photos-QDOJ1pyG' -%}
      {%- for item in site.photos reversed -%}
        {%- assign album = item.photos.album -%}
        {%- case p.lang -%}
          {%- when 'ca' -%}{%- assign t = item.title_ca -%}
          {%- when 'en' -%}{%- assign t = item.title_en -%}
          {%- when 'ja' -%}{%- assign t = item.title_ja -%}
          {%- else -%}{%- assign t = item.title_es -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
        {%- if album %}
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>{{ site.url }}/photos/{{ album }}/{{ album }}-0.jpg</image:loc>
      <image:title>{{ t | xml_escape }}</image:title>
    </image:image>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- elsif ref == 'classes-CJc2lhFv' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Same reason as the access branch below: the classes page renders its
        photographs from _data/classes.yml through a layout, so the generic
        branch cannot find the basenames in `p.content`.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- for d in site.data.classes.disciplines -%}
        {%- if d.image %}
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>{{ site.url }}/images/{{ d.image }}.jpg</image:loc>
      <image:title>{{ d.name[p.lang] | xml_escape }} · Aikido Musubi</image:title>
    </image:image>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- elsif ref == 'access-information-NdxqmVbV' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The access page renders its images from _data/venues.yml through the
        layout, so the generic branch below finds nothing: it looks for the
        basename in `p.content`, and the page's own content is only the intro
        paragraph. Read the data instead, the way the events branch does.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign V = site.data.venues -%}
      {%- for v in V.venues -%}
        {%- if v.plan %}
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>{{ site.url }}/images/{{ v.plan }}.jpg</image:loc>
      <image:title>{{ v.name[p.lang] | xml_escape }}</image:title>
    </image:image>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- for e in v.entrances %}
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>{{ site.url }}/images/{{ e.image }}.jpg</image:loc>
      <image:title>{{ v.name[p.lang] }} · {{ V.ui.entrance[p.lang] }} {{ e.letter }}, {{ e.street[p.lang] }}</image:title>
    </image:image>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign prefix = ref | append: "-" -%}
      {%- for f in content_images -%}
        {%- unless f.basename contains prefix %}{% continue %}{% endunless -%}
        {%- assign skip = false -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Only list images this page actually references. The basename appears
          verbatim in the page source whether or not Liquid has been expanded
          yet, so a substring test is reliable in both states.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- unless p.content contains f.basename %}{%- assign skip = true -%}{%- endunless -%}
        {%- comment -%} drop responsive hero variants — one page, one hero {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for v in hero_variants -%}
          {%- if f.basename contains v %}{%- assign skip = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- comment -%} drop the other languages' variants of the same image {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign tail = f.basename | split: "-" | last -%}
        {%- if known_langs contains tail and tail != p.lang %}{%- assign skip = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- unless skip %}
    <image:image>
      <image:loc>{{ site.url }}/images/{{ f.basename }}.jpg</image:loc>
    </image:image>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- for s in group %}
    <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ s.lang }}" href="{{ site.url }}{{ s.url }}" />
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if xdefault %}
    <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ site.url }}{{ xdefault.url }}" />
    {%- endif %}
  </url>
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
